**New evidence**
NSO 2022 nine-month household and labor conditions:
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Socio-economic situation in the third quarter and nine months of 2022","publisher":"National Statistics Office of Vietnam","publication_date":"2022-10","url":"https://www.nso.gov.vn/en/data-and-statistics/2022/10/socio-economic-situation-in-the-third-quarter-and-nine-months-of-2022/","claim":"In the first nine months of 2022, informal employment outside agriculture was estimated at 55.3% overall, with 47.0% in urban areas and 62.2% in rural areas; 83.2% of households said income was unchanged or increased versus the same period in 2021, while 16.8% reported income reduction, mostly due to Covid-19 and job-loss/input-cost shocks.","locator":"search result snippet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official national statistics article with exact percentages, but used from the search snippet because the page was not opened cleanly.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 nine-month household/labor data.","ruler_attribution":"Reflects economy-wide conditions under the Trọng-led party-state, but causation is shared with the PM, ministries, local governments, and external shocks rather than uniquely attributable to Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["High informal employment remained widespread, especially in rural areas.","A material minority of households still reported income declines."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.9","5B.10"]}

NSO 2022 living conditions by strata:
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Sự khác biệt về điều kiện sống giữa các tầng lớp dân cư ở Việt Nam năm 2022","publisher":"General Statistics Office of Vietnam","publication_date":"2023-11","url":"https://www.nso.gov.vn/tin-tuc-thong-ke/2023/11/su-khac-biet-ve-dieu-kien-song-giua-cac-tang-lop-dan-cu-o-viet-nam-nam-2022/","claim":"The 2022 household living-standards survey found per-capita monthly income of about 4.673 million VND; urban income was 5.945 million VND versus 3.864 million in rural areas; the richest quintile averaged 10.237 million VND versus 1.352 million for the poorest quintile; and the Southeast region had the highest average income while the Northern Midlands and Mountains had the lowest.","locator":"search result snippet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official statistical publication with specific distributional figures, but accessed through the search snippet because the page timed out on open.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 survey results published retrospectively in 2023.","ruler_attribution":"These are broad country outcomes shaped by national policy and structural geography; they do not isolate Trọng's personal contribution, but they do show the distributional pattern his system produced in 2022.","contrary_evidence":["Large urban-rural and top-bottom quintile gaps persisted.","Regional inequality remained pronounced."],"lenses":["5B.8","5B.10"]}

Viet Nam Social Security 2022 benefit delivery:
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Social and health insurance collection net to continue expanding","publisher":"Viet Nam Social Security","publication_date":"2022-06-01","url":"https://vss.gov.vn/english/news/Pages/vietnam-social-security.aspx?CateID=0&ItemID=10376","claim":"In 2022, the social insurance sector said coverage expanded to 92.04% of the population for health insurance and that it processed over 95,600 new benefit applications, timely paid pensions and monthly allowances to 3.3 million beneficiaries, and disbursed VND382 trillion in total benefits; it also said 99.3% of COVID-related support went by bank transfer.","locator":"lines 108-123","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Directly opened official agency page with explicit 2022 delivery figures and locator lines.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 implementation and disbursement evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Operationally attributable to the party-state under Trọng's leadership, but execution was shared with the social security agency and line ministries; the source does not prove personal micromanagement by Trọng.","contrary_evidence":["The agency also notes 4.9 million people were no longer eligible for HI support compared with end-2021 because of pandemic/policy changes.","Coverage expansion does not by itself prove equal access or quality."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.9"]}

Worker rent-support rollout:
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Hơn 2.400 lao động đầu tiên nhận hỗ trợ tiền thuê nhà","publisher":"Báo Điện tử Chính phủ","publication_date":"2022-05-26","url":"https://baochinhphu.vn/hon-2400-lao-dong-dau-tien-nhan-ho-tro-tien-thue-nha-102220526172921353.htm","claim":"By 20 May 2022, 55 of 61 provinces and cities had issued implementation plans for the worker rent-support policy, and the first two provinces had approved support for 2,431 workers totaling VND1.17 billion; delays were attributed to paperwork, social-security verification, and employers waiting to submit bundled three-month applications.","locator":"lines 181-193","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official government article with concrete rollout numbers and a clear implementation bottleneck explanation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 rollout evidence.","ruler_attribution":"The policy was a central-government measure under the Trọng era, but implementation was mainly through labor, social-security, and provincial administrative channels.","contrary_evidence":["Only two provinces had approved payments at the time of reporting.","The article itself says delays were still common because of paperwork and bundling behavior."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.9"]}

Economic-recovery package disbursement:
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Disbursement of economic recovery package remains slow","publisher":"Government News","publication_date":"2022-09-06","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/disbursement-of-economic-recovery-package-remains-slow-111220906161443877.htm","claim":"By January-August 2022, only VND55.5 trillion of the VND350 trillion economic recovery package had been disbursed; the package included VND10,073 billion in preferential loans, VND3.05 trillion in rent support for 4.54 million workers, and VND34.97 trillion in tax and fuel-tax waivers, and the minister said the low rate reflected complicated procedures and weak local initiative.","locator":"search result snippet","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government report with precise totals and implementation diagnosis, though the page itself was not opened successfully.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 implementation evidence.","ruler_attribution":"Strongly relevant to the Trọng-led governing system because the package was a central macro-recovery tool, but execution was shared with ministries and local authorities.","contrary_evidence":["Most of the package remained undisbursed at the reporting point.","The minister explicitly blamed procedures and local follow-through for the slowdown."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.7","5B.9","5B.10"]}

October 2022 government meeting:
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Government's regular meeting - October 2022","publisher":"Government News","publication_date":"2023-01-10","url":"https://en.baochinhphu.vn/governments-regular-meeting-october-2022-11123013120195868.htm","claim":"The Government's October 2022 resolution said public-investment disbursement and some Recovery Program policies still did not meet requirements, progress on planning remained slow, some people's lives were still difficult, wages and incomes remained low, and shortages of drugs, equipment, and medical supplies persisted at some medical facilities.","locator":"lines 197-199","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct opened official resolution text with explicit acknowledgement of implementation gaps and household hardship.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Late-2022 implementation/outcome evidence, published in early 2023.","ruler_attribution":"This is high-relevance system-level evidence under Trọng's leadership, but it attributes shortfalls primarily to the broader government apparatus rather than to Trọng personally.","contrary_evidence":["The same resolution also reports macro stability, recovery, and improving living standards.","It is an official self-assessment, so it may understate failures."],"lenses":["5B.9","5B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I checked the official statistics and implementation trail rather than adding more macro-only repeats. I retained 2022 household-income, distribution, social-security, rent-support, and recovery-disbursement sources because they directly address the gap. I did not add additional GDP/CPI/FDI-only pages because those are already covered in the existing evidence index and do not materially improve household-level or implementation-specific coverage. A direct open of two NSO pages timed out, so I used their search snippets instead. A few broader background items, including retrospective World Bank/ILO material, were considered but not needed because the official 2022 series now does the gap-closing work more directly.

**Remaining gaps**
Partly resolved. What is still thin is direct province-level audit data, household microdata, and tighter causal attribution from Trọng to the observed household and distribution outcomes rather than to the PM, ministries, provincial authorities, and external shocks. More search would help if you want to push this from partly resolved to fully documented, especially on provincial execution quality and bottom-quintile or ethnic-minority outcomes in 2022.
